# x-pad Cursor Rules

> Modular rules live in `.cursor/rules/`. Root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) is the handoff source of truth — keep it in sync when scripts, deps, or workflows change.

## Quick Context

**Project:** Cross-platform notepad (Notepad/Notepad++/Notepad4-style)
**Stack:** .NET 10 (`net10.0`), Avalonia UI 12, AvaloniaEdit + TextMate, CommunityToolkit.Mvvm
**UI:** Desktop Fluent theme; dark default; themes Dark / Light / System / Monokai / Hacker / AMOLED / GitHub
**Tests:** xUnit in `x-pad.Tests/`
**User data:** `%APPDATA%/XPad/` (`settings.json`, `session.json`, `layout.json`, `recovery/`, `crash.log`)

## Architecture (must preserve)

- **Views/** — Avalonia XAML + code-behind (thin)
- **ViewModels/** — state and commands (MVVM)
- **Services/** — file I/O, session, settings, LSP, AI, search, etc.
- **Editor/** — completion, indent, ghost text helpers
- **Models/** — `AppSettings`, snapshots, enums

## Non-negotiables

- `TextDocument` is source of truth — do not two-way bind large strings
- Dirty state via `UndoStack.IsOriginalFile` / `MarkAsOriginalFile()`
- All file I/O through `FileService` (encoding / BOM / EOL round-trip)
- Shortcuts via `KeyBindingCatalog` / `KeyBindingApplier` (not hard-coded `Window.KeyBindings`)
- Exclude `x-pad.Tests/**` from WinExe globs (`DefaultItemExcludes`)
- Log UI exceptions to `%APPDATA%/XPad/crash.log`; keep the process up
- Degrade gracefully (missing LSP, optional AI); never hardcode per-user paths

## Role prompts (optional)

Role playbooks live under `.cursor/prompts/`. Prefer adopting a role only when the task clearly matches; do not announce a role on every reply.

